<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>At the end of a jetty in Kilindini harbour, Mombasa, the depth of the water is <m>h</m> metres, <m>t</m> hours after midnight, where</p><p><me>h = {2.1} + {1.5}\sin\left(30(t - {7})\right)^\circ \quad\text{for } 0 \le t \le 24.</me></p><div>(a) Find the amplitude. <fillin characters="6" name="ans1"/> m  </div><div>(b) Find the period of the tide. <fillin characters="6" name="ans2"/> hours  </div><div>(c) At what time, in hours after midnight, is the first high tide? <fillin characters="6" name="ans3"/>  </div></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>(a) The water rises <m>{1.5}</m> m above its mean depth <m>{2.1}</m> m: the amplitude is <m>{1.5}</m> m.</p><p>(b) The angle grows by <m>30^\circ</m> every hour, and one complete wave is <m>360^\circ</m>: <m>360 \div 30 = 12</m> hours. The graph is drawn against time, so the repeat length is a period.</p><p>(c) The depth is greatest where <m>30(t - {7}) = 90</m>, so <m>t = {7} + 3 = {10}</m>. The first high tide is at <m>t = {10}</m>.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>1.5</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>12</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>10</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>